* zxtp25040dz.lib - Diodes Incorporated ZXTP25040DZ, 40 V PNP medium-power transistor, SOT-89.
* VENDOR MODEL, COPIED VERBATIM FROM THE MANUFACTURER'S OWN FILE.
*
* USAGE:
*   .include models/bjt_pnp/zxtp25040dz.lib
*   Q1 collector base emitter ZXTP25040DZ
*
* Role: CANDIDATE fast PNP for the complementary Class A emitter follower
* output stage (alternative to the MJE15033, whose model has CJE = 3.06 nF,
* NC-024/NC-025). Complement: ZXTN25040DZ (models/bjt_npn/zxtn25040dz.lib).
* NOT yet used by any circuit.
*
* PINOUT (datasheet DS33755 Rev. 2-2, page 1, top view pin-out figure;
* the figure carries no pin numbers): B / C / E on the three leads, the
* tab is COLLECTOR. Standard SOT-89 numbering is pin 1 = B, pin 2 = C
* (and tab), pin 3 = E - confirm against the KiCad footprint before layout.
*
* PROVENANCE - short version. Full record in
* models/bjt_pnp/zxtp25040dz.provenance.json and the freeze in
* vendor/bjt_pnp/diodes_inc/ZXTP25040DZ/PROVENANCE.json.
* Source: https://www.diodes.com/spice/download/2987/ZXTP25040DZ.spice.txt
* (Content-Type name="ZXTP25040DZ.spice.txt" checked, docs/limitations.md
* #21; header and .MODEL name read, #20). Frozen byte-for-byte, then
* appended below this header with NOTHING changed:
*
*   diff <(grep -v '^\*' vendor/bjt_pnp/diodes_inc/ZXTP25040DZ/ZXTP25040DZ.spice.txt) \
*        <(grep -v '^\*' models/bjt_pnp/zxtp25040dz.lib)      # empty
*
* The vendor file uses CRLF, this header uses LF: MIXED line endings on
* purpose, as in the other vendor-derived models. Do not normalise.
*
* CROSS-CHECK AGAINST THE DATASHEET (ngspice 47, set temp = 25, L46a):
*   fT   @ IC = -50 mA, VCE = -10 V, ftest = 100 MHz  275.9 MHz  (typ 270, no min)
*   fT   @ IC = -20 mA, VCE = -10 V (the follower)    194.1 MHz  (|hfe|=1: 194.1)
*   Cobo @ VCB = -10 V, 1 MHz                         18.10 pF   (typ 17.4, no max)
*   hFE  @ IC = -10 mA, VCE = -2 V                    414        (min 300, typ 450)
*   hFE  @ IC = -1 A,   VCE = -2 V                    295        (min 200, typ 300)
* The model lands on the datasheet TYPICALS; the datasheet publishes no
* fT minimum. WEAK POINT: VAF = 23 V and VAR = 4.5 V - a low forward Early
* voltage, so hFE and output conductance move noticeably with VCE over a
* +/-15 V swing. NO KF/AF in the model: NO 1/f noise. CJE = 183 pF,
* CJC = 58 pF at zero bias. QUASIMOD/RCO/GAMMA accepted by ngspice 47
* with no warning.
*
